    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193">

                <pb facs="0220" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg211"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">725:3515/16a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Attorney General</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cummings</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-06">May 6, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Attorney General</hi>: In pursuance of
                    our conversation over the telephone yesterday, I take pleasure in enclosing a
                    brief memorandum outlining the background and the salient features of the Beagle
                    Channel islands controversy between Argentina and Chile.</p>
                <pb facs="0221" n="212" xml:id="pg212"/>
                <p>I am gratified that you have accepted this exacting task. It is needless for me
                    to assure you that the full assistance of this Department is at your complete
                    disposal and I shall be most pleased to assist you in collecting publications,
                    data and maps that you may require.</p>
                <p>Believe me, with kindest regards as always,</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d193-a1.xml" xpointer="d193-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
